* POS(0) and RPOS(0) bound the command, and each digit SPAN requires a nonempty operand.
* The dot assignments capture the operation and operands only on success. :F(BAD) handles a failed match.
* IDENT compares the operation name as a string and :S(ADD) selects the addition branch.
    S = 'MUL(6,7)'
    P = POS(0) (('ADD' | 'MUL') . OP) '('
    P = P (SPAN('0123456789') . A) ','
    P = P (SPAN('0123456789') . B) ')' RPOS(0)
    S P :F(BAD)
    IDENT(OP,'ADD') :S(ADD)
    RESULT = A * B :(SHOW)
ADD RESULT = A + B
SHOW OUTPUT = 'Result: ' RESULT :(END)
BAD OUTPUT = 'invalid'
END
